"""Historical event master list (research period 2016-10-01 .. 2026-10-09).

Every event date / time comes from the cited sources (found via web search on 2026-10-11).
info_time_utc is the moment the information first became public, as precisely as the sources
allow; time_precision says how precise it is:
  EXACT    - a published time (e.g. "8 pm IST", "17:00 ET statement")
  APPROX   - time of day inferred from the sources (e.g. "early morning", "after US close")
  DATE_ONLY- only the date is known; treated as 00:00 UTC, so window 1 may include pre-news trading
Relevance columns are ANALYST JUDGEMENTS (subjective) - see README; measured severity is computed
separately from market data in compute.py.

Classification labels:
  A Black Swan candidate | B Major geopolitical shock | C Macroeconomic / monetary-policy shock
  D Financial-system crisis | E Commodity or supply-chain shock | F Other significant market-disrupting event
"""

